column59:
 "body": "I think the driver complains if the pin being configured is active high. In `gpio_pin_configure()` wrapper in `gpio.h` we have
```
if (((flags & GPIO_OUTPUT_INIT_LOGICAL) != 0)
    && ((flags & (GPIO_OUTPUT_INIT_LOW | GPIO_OUTPUT_INIT_HIGH)) != 0)
    && ((flags & GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW) != 0)) {
	flags ^= GPIO_OUTPUT_INIT_LOW | GPIO_OUTPUT_INIT_HIGH
		| GPIO_OUTPUT_INIT_LOGICAL;
}
```
which correctly flips `GPIO_OUTPUT_INIT_LOGICAL` flag only if pin is active low. If pin is active high the flag will be passed onto the driver."}

