 "body": "I changed `int ret = -1` to `int ret= -ENOTSUP` so there will be `-ENOTSUP` returned always if user tries to configure interrupt different than edge interrupt. Let me know if that's okay.

I don't think I am able to test this with `gpio_basic_api` since it requires to have `in-gpios` and `out-gpios` on the same GPIO port. I am using Arty A7 development board with LiteX SoC Builder. Unfortunately LiteX does not support interrupts on `GPIOInOut`. It is supported on `GPIOIn` only. That's what I was testing - multiple interrupts on multiple `GPIOIn` modules in `GPIO_INT_EDGE_RISING` or `GPIO_INT_EDGE_FALLING` modes. 
I've also tested it with `GPIO_INT_EDGE_BOTH` mode but since it is not supported by LiteX it works just like falling/rising edge mode depending on IRQ setup in LiteX `GPIOIn` module."}

