column93:
 "body": "The fix does not make sense for me. you did `(uint16_t_(f << 8)` to have  the same type of the left operand `(seed >> 8)`. Then the result of this operation will be an `uint16_t` that will be used as the left operand of  `^ (f << 3)` that is an `uint8_t`. Assuming that the evaluation happens from left to right. In resume;
```
(seed >> 8) ^ (uint16_t)(f << 8) ^ (f << 3) ^ (f >> 4);
 ->  (uint16_t) ^ (f << 3) ^ (f >> 4);
  -> (uint16_t) ^ (f >> 4);
   -> (uint16_t) ^ (uint8_t);
```

So it  seems to me that you have fixed **one** instance of the problem in this operation but the tool is not smart enough to understand it.
"}

