 a programming error that can go unnoticed if `pm_control` implementation does not write to `device_power_state` and the stack region happens to contain a value that corresponds to `PM_DEVICE_STATE_ACTIVE`.

There is a good reason why the existing implementation does `unsigned int device_power_state = 0;` -- i.e. doing so gets rid of any potential unpredictable behaviours.

This is a fairly standard practice and I don't see any reason why this should be an exception."}

