column88:
 but  with a buffer of size `RING_BUFFER_MAX_SIZE` (unlikely) this condition will result in calculations which overflow `uint32_t` in `ring_buf_is_empty()` and `ring_buf_size_get()`.

```
uint32_t ring_buf_size_get(struct ring_buf *buf)
{
	uint32_t tail = buf->tail;
	uint32_t head = buf->head;

	if (tail < head) {
		tail += get_rewind_value(buf->size

column89:
					 ring_buf_get_rewind_threshold());// get_rewind_value() can return RING_BUFFER_MAX_SIZE and result in tail overflow if buf->size==RING_BUFFER_MAX_SIZE
	}

	return tail - head;
}

```
Suggest only storing values in `buf->head` and `buf->tail` which are < rewind threshold.  The current implementation only considers rewinding `buf->tail` if its already past the rewind threshold _prior_ to adding elements.

Not sure if this is a real issue worth addressing."}

