into
```c
typedef struct {
    int32_t id;
    uint32_t cc_value;
    void *user_data;
    uint64_t expire_time;
} z_nrf_rtc_timer_compare_handler_param_t

typedef void (*z_nrf_rtc_timer_compare_handler_t)(const z_nrf_rtc_timer_compare_handler_param_t * param);
```
This way we will have `cc_value` preserved and also `expire_time` passed allowing to get rid of multiple calls to `z_nrf_rtc_timer_read` .

Or alternatively in `process_channel` we could have a global variable which could be read by a new getter let's call it say `z_nrf_rtc_expire_time_read()` from the cc handler. This way we could limit the number of calls to `z_nrf_rtc_timer_read` while having old information preserved.
@nordic-krch your opinion?
