column816:
 "body": "I thought that we have agreed that I shall use:
`if (littlefs_on_blkdev(mountp))` and then in the littlefs.h:

```
static inline bool littlefs_on_blkdev(struct fs_mount_t *mountp)
{
    if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_FS_LITTLEFS_BLK_DEV) && mountp->flags & FS_MOUNT_FLAG_USE_DISK_ACCESS)) {
           return true;
    }

    return false;
}
```

In that way the call to `littlefs_on_blkdev` will evaluate to an empty function and will be removed by LTO optimization.

Do you require to use the following pattern:
` if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_FS_LITTLEFS_BLK_DEV)  && littlefs_on_blkdev(mountp))` in the `littlefs_fs.c` mount function? 
So the `IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_FS_LITTLEFS_BLK_DEV)` will be used twice?

IMHO the approach proposed in this patch set is concise and neat."}

