```
p->ll_id = PDU_DATA_LLID_DATA_CONTINUE;
p->cp = 0U;
p->rfu = 0U;
```
should be optimized to single write operation. If there is a dependency on some variable e.g.
```
extern int foo;
p->ll_id = PDU_DATA_LLID_DATA_CONTINUE;
p->cp = foo;
p->rfu = 0U;
```
Then compiler will emit separate instructions to store `foo` value in `p->cp`.

